 "doubts": [
  "Annotations in views A, B, C are drawn in isometric planes (about 30 degrees); boxes are the axis-aligned box enclosing the rotated text or frame, so boxes of stacked items overlap.",
  "Frames and depth lines stacked under an nX callout carry that callout's multiplier (same convention as the d2mi hand keys).",
  "T4 is a two-row profile frame sharing one symbol cell (1.2|A|B|C over 0.2|A); one item per row, symbol repeated. STR1 3 COPLANAR SURFACES keyed as a note with multiplier 3, and T4 rows given multiplier 3 to match.",
  "D11, D12 (depth ↧35 ±1), D13 and STR3 INDICATED AREA form one stacked callout for the cross-drilled hole; each element keyed separately as the FSI lists them. D13 applies to a limited length shown by STR3.",
  "D10 and D15 are the counterbore depths under 4X ⌴ callouts (depth symbol written ↧).",
  "LDN1 (4X R0.2 MAX) and LDN2 (4X R0.15 MAX) are leader-directed notes that state radius limits; keyed as radius items with their LDN ids. LDN3 (F65, a feature label used by STR4) is excluded.",
  "STR4 AT SURFACE F65, STR5 AT BOTTOM OF COUNTERBORES and STR6 EACH LINE ELEMENT keyed as note items (they change where T19, T20, T24 apply).",
  "T22 straightness is a per-unit tolerance printed 0.2 / 15, written ⏤|0.2/15.",
  "T23 and T24 have an all-around circle on the leader (FSI: All Around); not in the frame text.",
  "Excluded: DF2, DF4, DF9 symbols, RLE1, RLE2, CS1-CS4."
 ],
